\details{
This function implements a nonparametric estimator for binary regression
based on the method of Signorini and Jones (2004). The estimator uses
kernel density estimation to estimate the conditional probability:

\deqn{P(Y=1|X=x) = \frac{n_1 f(x|Y=1)}{n_1 f(x|Y=1) + n_0 f(x|Y=0)}}

where \eqn{f(x|Y=1)} and \eqn{f(x|Y=0)} are kernel density estimates
for the predictor distributions in each response group, and \eqn{n_1},
\eqn{n_0} are the sample sizes in each group.

\strong{Visualization}:
\itemize{
\item For 1 predictor: creates a 2D plot showing data points and fitted curve
\item For 2 predictors: creates a 3D surface plot (requires \code{akima} package)
}

\strong{When to use}:
\itemize{
\item Binary response variable (logistic-type problems)
\item Want nonparametric alternative to logistic regression
\item Relationship between predictors and log-odds may be nonlinear
\item Small to moderate sample sizes (kernel methods can be unstable with sparse data)
}
